  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "Recommended for tanks 90–150 cm long, holding about 200–400 L",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "The seller pitches it for both planted tanks and fish-only tanks",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "The listing says the range works in both freshwater and saltwater, and suits beginners and experienced keepers alike",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "For smaller tanks the range offers RF-501 (40–80 cm) and RF-701 (60–90 cm)",
      "source": 0
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "Put the canister below the tank, fix the inlet and outlet hoses to the tank wall and tighten every joint to stop leaks",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "To prime, press the button on the lid repeatedly until water runs from the tank through the canister and back out of the outlet",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "One shop suggests priming by siphoning from the outlet instead of the button. It also says the filter restarts on its own after a power cut without re-priming",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "Keep the tank full and never run the unit dry",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "Cut off extra hose so it doesn't kink or tangle and cut the flow",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "The swivel connector turns 360°, and its lever both locks the hoses and sets the flow",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "The trays are different sizes, so each one has to go back in its original position",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Put coarse media at the bottom and finer media higher up, with a thin floss layer on top. Packing media too tightly makes water channel through it",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "Water moves up through all the trays from the bottom",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "Clean the trays regularly. Sellers give no fixed interval; clean the media and impeller when dirt builds up or the impeller clogs",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "The ceramic impeller shaft is fragile: take it out only if it is stuck, rinse it gently and don't drop it",
      "source": 2
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "The plastic latches can break if you force them while opening or closing the canister",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "One shop warns that bio balls make the unit noisy and let debris into the tray channels, and that the supplied ceramic rings hold few bacteria",
      "source": 2
    },
    {
      "fact": "If air gets in at the hose joints, replace the hose gasket",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Sources call RF-1301 the newer replacement for Atman's DF series (DF-1300). It has a refreshed design and is said to use less power",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Shops disagree on the specs: height is given as 42 or 47 cm, and hose size as 16 or 17 mm",
      "source": 5
    },
    {
      "fact": "Several shops show it as out of stock, so check availability before buying",
      "source": 2
    }
  ],
